From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 07:42:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] coremessaging: implement Windows.System.DispatcherQueue.

Office's React Native host asks for this class and, when the activation
factory is not there, throws winrt::hresult_class_not_registered with nothing
to catch it -- terminate, abort, and then Office's crash handler faulting in a
loop that burns a core for as long as Word stays up.  coremessaging registered
DispatcherQueueController but not the queue itself, so
RoGetActivationFactory(L"Windows.System.DispatcherQueue") failed outright.

A queue dispatches on exactly one thread, and the way to reach a thread that
pumps messages is to post it one, so each queue owns a message-only window on
its own thread and TryEnqueue posts the handler to it; the window procedure is
what runs on the far side.  That makes TryEnqueue real rather than a stub that
reports success -- tools/dqprobe enqueues a handler, pumps, and checks it ran.
GetForCurrentThread returns the calling thread's queue or NULL, which is what
the API says rather than an error, and HasThreadAccess compares thread ids.
CreateDispatcherQueueController now creates the queue instead of handing back
a controller with nothing behind it, and get_DispatcherQueue returns it.
CreateTimer and the shutdown events are still FIXMEs; DQTYPE_THREAD_DEDICATED
says so and uses the calling thread.

The class registration needs the DLL to self-register, so the spec exports the
winecrt0 DllRegisterServer and wine.inf registers coremessaging.

Measured against Word: activation failures for this class go from 4 per run to
0.  Two more classes it asks for are still missing --
Windows.Networking.Sockets.MessageWebSocket and
Windows.Web.Http.Filters.HttpBaseProtocolFilter -- and the second one is what
now precedes the crash loop.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 909fb02714e1d69b36a9eec16acc149dfb1c0caf)

